      "writtenOn": "2022-08-23T20:03:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Scratch my above comment because I was looking at the wrong patchset.\n\nBut I have a question on the suffix attribute itself. Shouldn\u0027t we err on the side of not having more attribute to the Bazel macros if possibe?\n\nInstead of adding suffix attribute, what\u0027s the drawback of having a BUILD like\n\n```\ncc_library_shared(\n  name  \u003d \"foo_shared\",\n  soname \u003d \"foo_shared-suf\", // or maybe \"\u003csoname\u003e-suf\"\n)\ncc_binary(\n  name \u003d \"foo-suf\", // if suffix: \"-suf\" in Android. \n)\n```\n?\n\nWith this approach, the soname (which makes use of the suffix) is more explicit in BUILD.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "0263a211_dce3bb86",
      "revId": "b78f4668989a0df171b2f2e08268e27e242f70b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "463c0047_811a9e37",
        "filename": "bp2build/cc_library_shared_conversion_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 664,
      "author": {
        "id": 1887575
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-23T20:10:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t disagree that having a separate \"suffix\" argument is less sensical than simply exposing `soname` outright. But we\u0027re just looking at migrating existing BPs, matching and minimizing differences while being idiomatic to Bazel. i.e., were this not migratory code, I\u0027d advocate for abstracting out to `soname` rather than just `suffix`.",
      "parentUuid": "862ef779_f2cfd3e6",
      "revId": "b78f4668989a0df171b2f2e08268e27e242f70b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d037dce_b1dd8a35",
        "filename": "bp2build/cc_library_shared_conversion_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 664,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-23T20:18:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We definitely need an attribute, not to change the name as this is often used in select statements, which would change the name.\n\nWe could consider using `soname`, but that could cause more repetition or complexity in BUILD files, given that these are often accompanied by select statements. E.g. a common case results in:\n\n```\ncc_binary(\n   name \u003d \"foo\",\n   suffix \u003d select({\n       \"//build/bazel/platforms/arch:x86\": \"-32\",\n       \"//build/bazel/platforms/arch:arm\": \"-32\",\n       \"//build/bazel/platforms/arch:x86_64\": \"-64\",\n       \"//build/bazel/platforms/arch:arm64\": \"-64\",\n   })\n)\n```\n\nwhich either requires `\"foo\" + select(...)` or repetition of `foo`",
      "parentUuid": "463c0047_811a9e37",
      "revId": "b78f4668989a0df171b2f2e08268e27e242f70b1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
